11. Calls for the withdrawal of the Asylum and Migration Pact, and the introduction of real and efficient controls at the Schengen borders; stresses that effective protection of the EU’s external borders is essential to prevent illegal immigration and for the proper functioning of the Schengen area, and is crucial for the security of the EU and its citizens; calls for the establishment of hubs outside the Schengen borders, where asylum seekers would await a decision on whether to be granted asylum or sent back to their country of arrival; calls for support from EU funds for the construction of physical barriers at the Schengen borders; underlines the need to strengthen the fight against criminal networks involved in migrant smuggling and trafficking and to address the EU’s vulnerability regarding the instrumentalisation of migrants as part of hybrid attacks;

